&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 300; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Working at Samsara means you’ll help define the future of physical operations and be on a team that’s shaping an exciting array of product solutions, including Video-Based Safety, Vehicle Telematics, Apps and Driver Workflows, and Equipment Monitoring. As part of a recently public company, you’ll have the autonomy and support to make an impact as we build for the long term.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Samsara is seeking a highly motivated people manager for our Operations Program Manager (OPM) team with a strong background in New Product Introduction (NPI) within the hardware manufacturing space. In this critical role, you will be managing a team of OPMs to ensure the successful operational launch of our cutting-edge products, from development through mass production and sustained volume. You will orchestrate complex cross-functional efforts, manage risks, and drive decisions that impact product cost, quality, and time to market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is a remote position based in the US. This position requires travel up to 20% of the time.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You should apply if:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You want to impact the industries that run our world:&lt;/strong&gt; Your efforts will result in real-world impact—helping to keep the lights on, get food into grocery stores, reduce emissions, and most importantly, ensure workers return home safely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are the architect of your own career:&lt;/strong&gt; If you put in the work, this role won’t be your last at Samsara. We set up our employees for success and have built a culture that encourages rapid career development, countless opportunities to experiment and master your craft in a hyper growth environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’re energized by our opportunity:&lt;/strong&gt; The vision we have to digitize large sectors of the global economy requires your full focus and best efforts to bring forth creative, ambitious ideas for our customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You want to be with the best:&lt;/strong&gt; At Samsara, we win together, celebrate together and support each other. You will be surrounded by a high-calibre team that will encourage you to do your best.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a global Operations Program Management team based in North America and Asia to develop and launch new hardware products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end operational execution of hardware product manufacturing from concept through mass production and sustained volume.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary operations liaison, aligning and communicating across Engineering, Product, Supply Chain, Manufacturing, and other cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop comprehensive program plans, manage schedules, budgets, and proactively mitigate risks to ensure on-time and on-cost delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and execute manufacturing strategies, collaborating with internal teams and external partners for factory readiness, capacity, and process development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive cost reduction initiatives and ensure robust quality standards are met throughout the product lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion, role model, and embed Samsara’s cultural principles (Focus on Customer Success, Build for the Long Term, Adopt a Growth Mindset, Be Inclusive, Win as a Team) as we scale globally and across new offices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements for the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Engineering (Mechanical, Electrical, Industrial, or Manufacturing preferred), Supply Chain Management, or a related technical field. A master&#39;s degree (MBA or MS) is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of progressive experience in Operations Program Management, NPI, or related roles within a hardware manufacturing environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 3 years managing a team of at least 4 individuals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of successfully launching multiple complex hardware products from concept to high-volume production and strong understanding of hardware development lifecycles and manufacturing processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert-level proficiency in program/project management methodologies and tools (e.g., Confluence/JIRA). PMP certification is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional leadership, communication, and interpersonal skills with the ability to influence and align diverse cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly analytical with a strong ability to identify problems, analyze data, and develop effective solutions in a fast-paced, ambiguous environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with global manufacturing partners and supply chains. Willingness to travel internationally as required (up to 20%).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meticulous attention to detail and a commitment to operational excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An ideal candidate also has:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with PLM (Product Lifecycle Management) systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in dash camera, gateway, or telematics products is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
