&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You want to impact the industries that run our world:&lt;/strong&gt; Your efforts will result in real-world impact – helping to keep the lights on, get food into grocery stores, reduce emissions, and most importantly, ensure workers return home safely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are the architect of your own career:&lt;/strong&gt; If you put in the work, this role won’t be your last at Samsara. We set up our employees for success and have built a culture that encourages rapid career development, countless opportunities to experiment and master your craft in a hyper growth environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’re energized by our opportunity:&lt;/strong&gt; The vision we have to digitize large sectors of the global economy requires your full focus and best efforts to bring forth creative, ambitious ideas for our customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You want to be with the best:&lt;/strong&gt; At Samsara, we win together, celebrate together and support each other. You&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;will be surrounded by a high-calibre team that will encourage you to do your best.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver accurate, consistent security assessments of Samsara&#39;s software, code,&amp;nbsp; and firmware, evaluating their resilience against AI-driven/adversarial attacks, and implementing fixes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and translate&amp;nbsp; general AI security findings into Samsara-specific fixes for our application security layer— including adapting techniques built for software to apply to hardware and embedded firmware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Find both AI-specific and traditional vulnerabilities (e.g., injection, IDOR) using AI-driven offensive validation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and pressure-test novel AI-enabled security tooling and workflows, then drive adoption of what proves valuable across the broader security org.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Benchmark each new frontier model against the previous one for security tasks, and build the release criteria and guardrails for adopting it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support AppSec vulnerability triage through an office-hours rotation, and help run our bug bounty program, with potential expansion to hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with engineering, hardware, and leadership.&amp;nbsp; Present findings to security and executive leadership&amp;nbsp; as Samsara&#39;s go-to expert on AI-related security risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help define &amp;amp; drive&amp;nbsp; Samsara&#39;s medium- and long-term strategy for adopting AI safely and effectively within security operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use frontier AI/LLM tools (e.g., Anthropic&#39;s and OpenAI&#39;s cybersecurity-specific programs) hands-on for both offensive validation (red-teaming our own systems) and defensive tooling — required experience integrating, securing, or red-teaming AI-enabled systems (e.g., LLMs, agentic workflows, prompt injection/adversarial testing) is essential to this role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion, role model, and embed Samsara’s cultural principles (Focus on Customer Success, Build for the Long Term, Adopt a Growth Mindset, Be Inclusive, Win as a Team) as we scale globally and across new offices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements for the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in application security, vulnerability management, threat modeling, offensive security, or a closely related discipline, with demonstrated application fix impact and influence across a large part of an organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building AI or agentic workflows for security use cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience conducting technical security assessments (e.g. offensive security or validation exercises) across both software and hardware/firmware environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in creating solutions for secure code with engineers using languages such as GoLang.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing AI and agentic solutions using Github, and developing within AWS cloud.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An ideal candidate also has:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AI-specific attack techniques (prompt injection, jailbreaks, model/agent abuse) for vulnerability management and application security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or validating security controls for agentic AI, RAG systems, or LLM-integrated platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience red-teaming LLM-enabled systems (prompt injection, agent abuse).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience evaluating or benchmarking LLMs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bug bounty platform experience (e.g., Bugcrowd).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in federal or FedRAMP-style environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of driving org-wide security strategy or presenting technical findings to senior/executive stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant industry certifications (e.g., OSCP, GIAC, CISSP) or AWS certifications.&lt;/li&gt;
